structured_output.question:
Muon reversed the earlier SGD evidence. On the block conv filters it gave about +0.7-0.8 pp at equal epochs (E025, E026). It now carries the tip, E031: 8.75 epochs, batch 2048, 5.43 s, 0.7551, with a thin margin. Near 9-10 epochs, cutting epochs costs only ~0.3 pp per epoch, while resize and stronger augmentation both hurt under Muon (E029, E030). So the next time cut needs more accuracy per epoch from the optimizer itself. Which Muon-family changes raise sample efficiency in very short training (<= 10 epochs) of small convnets at large batch, at little or no extra per-step cost? Candidates:
- momentum and lr settings, and how they scale with batch size;
- the number of Newton-Schulz iterations and their coefficients (e.g. Polar Express, quintic variants);
- weight decay under Muon;
- the lr schedule shape and warmup under Muon;
- which parameters Muon should cover (first conv, head, BN);
- normalized or adaptive variants (NorMuon, AdaMuon, Dion);
- interaction with Lookahead, EMA or label smoothing.
